# interpretation / caveats
pre='Q12: '
r['interpretation']=r['interpretation'].split(' | Q12:')[0]+(' | Q12 (round 2): the three low-resolution sets (Xb55, Xb4f, Xb47) are ACA data. Their relative filtering is NOT measured: bowl depths (3-6% of peak) are not ordered with wavelength, the cleaned-map integral is not zero (so the bowl is not a missing-flux estimator), and a forward model with cleaning does not give R55>=R4f>=R47. The loss-only extrapolation (R55/R4f 1.05-1.18 at the centre, R47/R4f 0.89-0.97) is a prior-conditional systematic budget item of <=10% at the centre, below the 10% per-band calibration; the claim that T(2-1)/T(3-2)>1 and T(4-3)/T(3-2)<<1 at the nuclei is thus a statement about calibration, not about recovery. After removing nuclear contamination, the clump E1 is compact and fully recovered by the 12-m array (Xb4d/Xb4f 1.0) while W is extended (0.3); the disk T21/T32 excess at E1 vanishes against the nuclear complex (0.96), the HCN 4-3/3-2 disk deficit (E1, W) and the HCO+ 4-3/3-2 deficit at W survive. Same-J HCN/HCO+ ratios at N,S,Bridge are robust to recovery at <=10%.')
cv=[c for c in r['caveats'] if not c.startswith('Q12:')]
cv.append('Q12: absolute losses of every array are not measurable without total-power/short-spacing data (cleaned-image integrals equal the clean-component flux, not zero); simulated ACA losses at r<8" are 10-30% for plausible skies but depend on assumed uv coverage, sky and clean parameters. MRS ratios (0.30 [0.20,0.45]) are nominal. The loss-only extrapolation to Xb55/Xb47 is conditional on its priors and the forward model does not reproduce its ordering. Clump fluxes depend on the assumed Gaussian clump shape (FWHM 1.5-4"), the halo decomposition and, for E2 and the HCN clumps, are not constrained (blending with the S halo; clumps below 3 sigma). The Xb47 field (+-25") ends before its bowl closes.')
r['caveats']=cv
for x in r['results']:
    if x['confidence'] not in ('high','medium','low'): x['confidence']='low'   # schema allows only high/medium/low ('tentative' in 3 older entries)
